    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105-a2">

                <pb facs="0269" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg197"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 316.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Berry to Mr.
                            Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >House of Representatives</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 6, 1882</date>.
                        (Received February 8.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Inclosed is a letter of Daniel
                    McSweeny, formerly a resident of California, but now in Dundalk jail, Ireland.
                    The letter is addressed to his daughter now living in San Francisco.</p>
                <p>His seems a hard case, and even were he justly imprisoned, he certainly is
                    entitled to humane treatment. I call your special attention to the letter.</p>
                <p>The appeals of his personal friends in California to me must be my excuse for
                    thus addressing you.</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. P. BERRY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
